#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-daemon.md:46
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-daemon.md:48
msgid ""
"This command runs the Nix daemon, which is a required component in multi-"
"user Nix installations. It runs build tasks and other operations on the Nix "
"store on behalf of non-root users. Usually you don't run the daemon "
"directly; instead it's managed by a service management framework such as "
"`systemd` on Linux, or `launchctl` on Darwin."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-daemon.md:54
msgid "Note that this daemon does not fork into the background."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-daemon.md:56
msgid "Socket path"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-daemon.md:58
msgid ""
"Unless `--stdio` is used, the daemon listens on a Unix domain socket. The "
"socket path is determined similarly as for the [Local Daemon Store](../../"
"store/types/local-daemon-store.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-daemon.md:61
msgid "The `--socket-path` flag, if passed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-daemon.md:63
msgid ""
"The [`NIX_DAEMON_SOCKET_PATH`](../../command-ref/env-common.md#env-"
"NIX_DAEMON_SOCKET_PATH) environment variable, if set."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-daemon.md:65
msgid ""
"Otherwise, `daemon-socket/socket` within the store's state directory. The "
"[Local Store](../../store/types/local-store.md), [Local Daemon Store](../../"
"store/types/local-daemon-store.md), and [Experimental SSH Store with "
"filesystem mounted](../../store/types/experimental-ssh-store-with-filesystem-"
"mounted.md) each have their own per-store state directory. For other store "
"types, the global [`NIX_STATE_DIR`](../../command-ref/env-common.md#env-"
"NIX_STATE_DIR) is used."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-daemon.md:75
msgid "Systemd socket activation"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-daemon.md:77
msgid ""
"`nix daemon` supports systemd socket-based activation using the `nix-daemon."
"socket` unit in the Nix distribution. It supports listening on multiple "
"addresses; for example, the following stanza in `nix-daemon.socket` makes "
"the daemon listen on two Unix domain sockets:"
msgstr ""

